WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.333
Luke, Chapter Twenty.

2
00:00:01.333 --> 00:00:14.933
And it came to pass, that on one of those days, as he taught the people in the temple, and preached the gospel, the chief priests and the scribes came upon him with the elders, And spake unto him, saying, Tell us, by what authority doest thou these things?

3
00:00:14.933 --> 00:00:17.867
or who is he that gave thee this authority?

4
00:00:17.867 --> 00:00:26.533
And he answered and said unto them, I will also ask you one thing; and answer me: The baptism of John, was it from heaven, or of men?

5
00:00:26.533 --> 00:00:34.133
And they reasoned with themselves, saying, If we shall say, From heaven; he will say, Why then believed ye him not?

6
00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:41.467
But and if we say, Of men; all the people will stone us: for they be persuaded that John was a prophet.

7
00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:45.467
And they answered, that they could not tell whence it was.

8
00:00:45.467 --> 00:00:50.667
And Jesus said unto them, Neither tell I you by what authority I do these things.

9
00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:59.733
Then began he to speak to the people this parable; A certain man planted a vineyard, and let it forth to husbandmen, and went into a far country for a long time.

10
00:00:59.733 --> 00:01:07.867
And at the season he sent a servant to the husbandmen, that they should give him of the fruit of the vineyard: but the husbandmen beat him, and sent him away empty.

11
00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:15.067
And again he sent another servant: and they beat him also, and entreated him shamefully, and sent him away empty.

12
00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:20.267
And again he sent a third: and they wounded him also, and cast him out.

13
00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:23.467
Then said the lord of the vineyard, What shall I do?

14
00:01:23.467 --> 00:01:28.400
I will send my beloved son: it may be they will reverence him when they see him.

15
00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:36.933
But when the husbandmen saw him, they reasoned among themselves, saying, This is the heir: come, let us kill him, that the inheritance may be ours.

16
00:01:36.933 --> 00:01:39.733
So they cast him out of the vineyard, and killed him.

17
00:01:39.733 --> 00:01:43.200
What therefore shall the lord of the vineyard do unto them?

18
00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:47.200
He shall come and destroy these husbandmen, and shall give the vineyard to others.

19
00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.733
And when they heard it, they said, God forbid.

20
00:01:49.733 --> 00:01:58.400
And he beheld them, and said, What is this then that is written, The stone which the builders rejected, the same is become the head of the corner?

21
00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:05.200
Whosoever shall fall upon that stone shall be broken; but on whomsoever it shall fall, it will grind him to powder.

22
00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:15.333
And the chief priests and the scribes the same hour sought to lay hands on him; and they feared the people: for they perceived that he had spoken this parable against them.

23
00:02:15.333 --> 00:02:26.800
And they watched him, and sent forth spies, which should feign themselves just men, that they might take hold of his words, that so they might deliver him unto the power and authority of the governor.

24
00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:39.467
And they asked him, saying, Master, we know that thou sayest and teachest rightly, neither acceptest thou the person of any, but teachest the way of God truly: Is it lawful for us to give tribute unto Caesar, or no?

25
00:02:39.467 --> 00:02:44.000
But he perceived their craftiness, and said unto them, Why tempt ye me?

26
00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.467
Shew me a penny.

27
00:02:45.467 --> 00:02:47.867
Whose image and superscription hath it?

28
00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:51.867
They answered and said, Caesar's.

29
00:02:51.867 --> 00:02:59.200
And he said unto them, Render therefore unto Caesar the things which be Caesar's, and unto God the things which be God's.

30
00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:05.200
And they could not take hold of his words before the people: and they marvelled at his answer, and held their peace.

31
00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:21.867
Then came to him certain of the Sadducees, which deny that there is any resurrection; and they asked him, Saying, Master, Moses wrote unto us, If any man's brother die, having a wife, and he die without children, that his brother should take his wife, and raise up seed unto his brother.

32
00:03:21.867 --> 00:03:26.800
There were therefore seven brethren: and the first took a wife, and died without children.

33
00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:30.400
And the second took her to wife, and he died childless.

34
00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:36.667
And the third took her; and in like manner the seven also: and they left no children, and died.

35
00:03:36.667 --> 00:03:39.200
Last of all the woman died also.

36
00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:42.267
Therefore in the resurrection whose wife of them is she?

37
00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:44.400
for seven had her to wife.

38
00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:59.200
And Jesus answering said unto them, The children of this world marry, and are given in marriage: But they which shall be accounted worthy to obtain that world, and the resurrection from the dead, neither marry, nor are given in marriage: Neither can they die any more:

39
00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:05.867
for they are equal unto the angels; and are the children of God, being the children of the resurrection.

40
00:04:05.867 --> 00:04:14.533
Now that the dead are raised, even Moses shewed at the bush, when he calleth the Lord the God of Abraham, and the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob.

41
00:04:14.533 --> 00:04:19.733
For he is not a God of the dead, but of the living: for all live unto him.

42
00:04:19.733 --> 00:04:24.667
Then certain of the scribes answering said, Master, thou hast well said.

43
00:04:24.667 --> 00:04:28.133
And after that they durst not ask him any question at all.

44
00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:32.533
And he said unto them, How say they that Christ is David's son?

45
00:04:32.533 --> 00:04:41.467
And David himself saith in the book of Psalms, The LORD said unto my Lord, Sit thou on my right hand, Till I make thine enemies thy footstool.

46
00:04:41.467 --> 00:04:45.200
David therefore calleth him Lord, how is he then his son?

47
00:04:45.200 --> 00:05:02.133
Then in the audience of all the people he said unto his disciples, Beware of the scribes, which desire to walk in long robes, and love greetings in the markets, and the highest seats in the synagogues, and the chief rooms at feasts; Which devour widows' houses, and for a shew make long prayers:

48
00:05:02.133 --> 00:05:04.800
the same shall receive greater damnation.

